{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler orchestrator) assigned task #5362: implement srd039-env requirements R3.3, R4.1, R4.2, R4.3 for the `cmd/env` utility. This is a \"stitch\" task in a code generation pipeline. The task requires:\n   - Modifying `cmd/env/main.go` to add R3.3 functionality (error handling for invalid options with exit 125)\n   - Modifying `cmd/env/env_test.go` to add differential tests for R3.3, R4.1, R4.2, R4.3\n   - Preserving all existing code for R1.1-R3.2\n   - Ensuring differential tests pass against the `genv` reference binary\n   - No git commands allowed (managed externally by orchestrator)\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary against GNU reference binary (`genv`)\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - GNU env utility behavior: `-i` (ignore environment), `-u` (unset), `-0` (NUL-delimited output), `NAME=VALUE` pairs\n   - Exit codes: 125 for invalid options, 126 for permission denied, 127 for command not found\n   - Test normalizers: `sortLines`, `sortNulLines`, `normalizeBinaryName` for handling output ordering differences\n   - Go module: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd039-env.yaml** (SRD - read for requirements)\n     - R3.3: \"Must print an error message to stderr when an invalid option is given and exit 125.\"\n     - R4.1: \"Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (genv) via pkg/testutils.\"\n     - R4.2: \"Tests must cover: no-argument environment dump, NAME=VALUE setting, -u unsetting, -i empty environment, -0 NUL-delimited output, COMMAND execution with modified env, and exit code passthrough.\"\n     - R4.3: \"Tests must verify error output and exit code for invalid options and missing commands.\"\n     - Non-goals: No -C (chdir), -S (split string), no stdin reading, no shell expansion.\n\n   - **cmd/env/main.go** (existing implementation, 183 lines)\n     - Already implements R1.1-R3.2\n     - Package comment: `// Implements srd039-env R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, R3.1, R3.2.`\n     - Key functions: `main()`, `parseShortFlags()`, `buildEnv()`, `removeVar()`, `countAssignments()`, `printEnv()`, `execCommand()`, `isNotFound()`\n     - Invalid option handling at lines 62-65: `fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"env: invalid option -- '%s'\\n\", arg)` then `os.Exit(125)` — this partially implements R3.3 but the error message format may not match GNU env exactly\n     - Uses `errors.AsType[*exec.ExitError]` (line 173) for exit code extraction\n     - The `parseShortFlags` function returns `(\"\", false)` for unknown flags, triggering the error path\n\n   - **cmd/env/env_test.go** (existing tests, 227 lines)\n     - Has `TestDiff` with 28 test cases covering R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, R3.1, R3.2\n     - Has `command_not_found` test (exit code 127) with `normalizeBinaryName` normalizer\n     - Missing: tests for invalid options (R3.3/R4.3), e.g., `env --bogus` or `env -z`\n     - Helper functions: `findEnvBin()`, `normalizeBinaryName()`, `sortLines()`, `sortNulLines()`\n     - `normalizeBinaryName` replaces \"genv:\" with \"env:\" to normalize error messages between Go and reference binaries\n\n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (provided in prompt context)\n     - `DiffTest` struct with fields: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n     - `RunDiffTests` runs each test case comparing Go and reference binaries\n     - `buildEnv` sets LC_ALL=C by default\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — I had just finished reading the three required files and was about to begin implementation when the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that R3.3 (invalid option error + exit 125) is already partially implemented in main.go lines 62-65, but the error message format needs to be verified against GNU env's actual output for differential testing to pass.\n   - Identified that R4.1/R4.2 are largely covered by existing tests, but R4.3 specifically requires tests for invalid options and missing commands — the missing commands test exists but invalid options tests do not.\n   - The key gap: need to add test cases for invalid options (e.g., `--bogus`, `-z`) that verify stderr output and exit code 125, with appropriate normalizers for binary name differences.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The full task prompt with role, repository_files, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source_code, requirement_states), context (task 5362), execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task instructions, constraints, description, shared_protocols, and package_contracts.\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement R3.3: Verify/fix error message format for invalid options to match GNU env (`genv`) output exactly\n   - Implement R4.3: Add differential test cases for invalid options (e.g., `env --bogus`, `env -z`) verifying stderr and exit code 125\n   - Ensure R4.1 and R4.2 test coverage is complete (most already exists)\n   - Update the package comment in main.go to include R3.3, R4.1, R4.2, R4.3\n   - Run `go build ./cmd/env/`, `go vet ./cmd/env/`, and `go test ./cmd/env/ -count=1` to verify\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three required files (srd039-env.yaml, cmd/env/main.go, cmd/env/env_test.go) and was about to plan and implement the changes. Specifically:\n   \n   The existing `cmd/env/main.go` already