 We need a broader approach since the current normalizer only replaces the first \"genv:\" occurrence. I'll create a function that replaces all instances of \"genv\" with \"env\" throughout the output, which should handle both the error message and the help text suggestion.\n\nWriting normalizer function... not \"-i\"/\"--ignore-environment\", not \"-0\"/\"--null\", not \"-u\", doesn't start with \"--unset=\" — so it reaches the long option handling, which should print `env: invalid option -- 'bogus'\\n` and exit with code 2.\n\nThe core issue is that `parseShortFlags` needs to return the invalid character so the error message shows just `z` instead of `-z`, and I need to handle long options similarly by extracting the option name after the dashes.\n\nRefactoring the error handling...\n\nI need to check for unrecognized long options (those starting with `--`) before calling `parseShortFlags`, and output the correct error message with the \"Try\" line. Then I'll modify `parseShortFlags` to properly identify which character in a short flag sequence is invalid, so I can distinguish between short and long option errors. I need to handle unrecognized long options and make sure all error messages consistently include the \"Try 'env --help'\" line, plus fix the `-u` missing argument case to match that pattern. Let me map out the changes needed in main.go to align with how the reference implementation behaves.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3134,"cache_read_input_tokens":28284,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3134},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7fd77e31-8049-4555-8986-4c4990e0d15f","uuid":"40efda99-67d3-4ae6-8e61-19b083daf379"}
